From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HarnessOS <patches@harnessos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: build local artifacts with exact source provenance

Since v1.4.221 build:cli runs upstream's prepare:cli-output, which here stops at
verify-cli-bin: a build never symlinks the dev CLI into /usr/local/bin. The
Windows dev-channel publish assertions go with publish: null, as the
uninstaller-hook test upstream retired does.

Carried-Because: Local builds carry exact source provenance, sign only with the identity they are given, and never publish to upstream.
Tests: config/scripts/build-provenance.test.mjs, config/scripts/electron-builder-mac-channel-config.test.mjs and affected packaging gates.

